    <statement><p>Given <m>u(x,t)=\frac{1}{t}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}</m>, compute:</p>
<p><m>u_{xx}=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}+0.25\frac{1}{t^{3}}x^{2}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>u_{x}=\frac{1}{t} \frac{\partial}{\partial{x}} e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}=\frac{2x}{4t} \frac{1}{t} e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}=0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}xe^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}</m>



We now differentiate <m>u_{x}</m> with respect to <m>x</m>, using the Product Rule and the Chain Rule.



<m>u_{xx}=0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}+0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}x \frac{\partial}{\partial{x}} e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}=0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}+0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}x \cdot \frac{2x}{4t} e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}=0.5\frac{1}{t^{2}}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}+0.25\frac{1}{t^{3}}x^{2}e^{\frac{x^{2}}{4t}}</m>





</solution>
